1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,737
Every Seeker came with an address, and nobody ever writes to it.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,997
So we built Penny Post, a letterbox for your wallet.

3
00:00:09,247 --> 00:00:14,216
Every morning it brings one question for everyone, and everyone who answers shares the pot.

4
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:21,194
It brings postcards too. A stranger pays your price to reach you, and you keep ninety percent.

5
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,686
If you never open it, their money goes back to them.

6
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,394
A paid message is only a gate on a chat.

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,297
This is the post, and it comes once a day.

8
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:55,026
Here is the real app, live on Solana devnet. You don't even need a wallet to try it. Choose the practice wallet, tap Set me up, and that one tap gives you a letterbox. A few seconds later the morning post arrives: today's question, and a welcome card.

9
00:00:57,871 --> 00:01:02,190
If you bring your own wallet, every signature goes through Mobile Wallet Adapter.

10
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:26,027
Let me open today's question. Somebody asked every Seeker, tea or coffee first thing, and put up 300 SKR for whoever answers. I pick tea, and approve once. The program checks my Seeker Genesis Token on-chain, so one phone gets exactly one answer. And I'm in. My share so far is 45 SKR.

11
00:01:28,994 --> 00:01:53,746
Now it is the next morning. Yesterday's question has closed, tea won, and my share is waiting for me. There is a new question as well. With a single signature, I collect yesterday's SKR and answer today's. That is the whole habit: one tap each morning, and it pays you. For this scene, we moved the test clock forward one day.

12
00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:19,407
The rest of the post comes from people. Here, a stranger has paid my price, 10 SKR, to send me a card. Their money sits in escrow. I can see who it is from, and nothing more, until I sign for it. When I do, the card slides out of its envelope, turns over, and 9 SKR is mine. If I had ignored it for a week, they would have got their money back.

13
00:02:23,795 --> 00:02:35,683
I can write back. I write the message with my finger, choose a stamp, and the app tells me what it costs, and when it will arrive, before I sign anything. The card is sealed, so only their phone can read it.

14
00:02:42,004 --> 00:02:49,388
On my profile, I set my own price. And any builder can ask every Seeker tomorrow's question, simply by putting up the pot.

15
00:02:52,244 --> 00:03:05,526
That is Penny Post. It is live on Solana devnet today, with an app anyone can install, tested against real SKR and real Seeker Genesis Tokens. The post comes once a day.
